   word's text-decoration underline — the pitch/status signal — does not paint
   into it. That left only bare-kana remainders underlined while every kanji run
   carrying a reading lost the line (reported on YouTube: "only hiragana and
   katakana words get the underline"). Give the box the word's own underline so
   the line runs under the whole word. The .jpdb-reader-detached-furi child is
